r-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">Write a Java program using synchronized threads, which demonstrates producer consumerconcept.</p><p data-ref="bea63862-3c04-414a-8c7e-a151830531f9" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="5d3e610a-4d06-415d-aae0-c3379bca4d9c"></p><p data-ref="9671e4f9-4cb0-451c-9d80-72951451f901" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">The Producer-Consumer problem is a classic synchronization problem in computer science. It involves two types of threads:</p><ul data-ref="b7ab2666-a3e4-40d9-9561-3a1a9c26ecbe" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><li data-ref="733e198f-4db2-4826-bf3f-da59ed641315"><strong data-ref="6410241c-d0c9-460e-a7ef-299f690a84c2">Producer</strong>: This thread generates data (e.g., items) and places it in a shared resource (like a buffer).</li><li data-ref="b3e6b15f-df0c-41aa-94ae-e7b0a99da41b"><strong data-ref="f780eae8-cfa4-4ba5-9d5a-96206d60077d">Consumer</strong>: This thread takes data (items) from the shared resource for processing or consumption.</li></ul><p data-ref="a9fcc280-a56f-4362-9867-2054cf37a80c" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="4dc98133-57f0-4f45-b63b-1649f7dd451c"></p><p data-ref="a28b7787-2621-4df0-95af-0ebc0aaad8a3" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">The problem revolves around coordinating these threads such that:</p><ul data-ref="11c8dca2-ec9b-4d4d-8a19-86fd76bd096a" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><li data-ref="2781deef-8220-460d-a117-d5a9eca21598">The producer does not produce when the buffer is full.</li><li data-ref="e6179143-4413-448a-b44f-699689fd8bae">The consumer does not consume when the buffer is empty.</li><li data-ref="9f47a806-ace7-49d9-9860-112a335a4c9e">Both threads operate safely without corrupting the shared resource.</li></ul><p data-ref="3fdd6ab8-670d-4444-8be3-5825cc8d03a9" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="9fcd664a-d627-4dea-8297-5235bc3c64ec"></p><p data-ref="1dffeeb9-4488-4c15-a013-7378af7535fc" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">To achieve synchronization in Java, we can use the synchronized keyword along with wait and notify methods to control the interaction between the threads.</p><p data-ref="c95bfc7a-f9ea-4d2f-b65d-dbb762dfb71a" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="8d4eba5a-2193-40d3-8f8e-f3a7f13a12a6"></p><p data-ref="763eb5b6-d25c-466f-aac7-857b18e0db61" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><strong data-ref="cfa3bec0-02dc-4c77-a116-34bf79ea5f98">Input Format:</strong></p><ul data-ref="296e0739-fe92-4162-b860-be337b0dbae1" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><li data-ref="312dcc56-2a6b-4051-a894-4add4b6ba65f">Prompt the user to enter an integer representing the number of items to produce along with a print statement <strong data-ref="1cfc52f3-912b-4acd-a243-1c84c1037c0d">"Enter the number of items to produce: " </strong></li></ul><p data-ref="f0e17f14-fd91-4eae-9166-eb9773ef4845" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="48c9dae7-f73b-42c9-aaae-98d384315b3c"></p><p data-ref="7ba14948-50f8-42a0-b10f-db105164fb57" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><strong data-ref="2549e548-b838-4f3b-ba52-db567a95e524">Output Format:</strong></p><p data-ref="359f05ac-56cd-4fe9-abb6-2953f51bee5c" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">Output should print the following:</p><ul data-ref="4d1e9cfa-13f9-470b-a75f-dba49898f839" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><li data-ref="9f336479-9297-4702-a838-debdb0a05f79">Messages indicating the production of each item as &lt;Produced: {Produced item}&gt;</li><li data-ref="0c67a60c-b4d0-4c00-819c-e3b5c5e66b0a">Messages indicating the consumption of each item as &lt;Consumed: {Consumed item}&gt;</li></ul></span></div><div class="mb-3" data-ref="dc929e68-8b6a-4840-9828-7f9363736f57"><div class="ml-1 mb-3" data-ref="66100e58-79fb-4fb3-9eb9-83597ec6cfbd"><b style="border-bottom:1px solid black;" data-ref="534e6904-7da5-4b52-b495-a0830e5aae3f" data-undisplayed="undisplayed">Source Code: </b></div><div class="user-solution" style="page-break-inside: auto" data-ref="179c2d7a-59f7-40d1-abdb-af27f3ee8b73" data-undisplayed="undisplayed"><div class="px-3 pt-2 pb-1" style="font-family: monospace !important;border-radius: 4px 4px 0 0; border: 1px solid black; break-after: avoid; page-break-after: avoid;" data-ref="a4959051-17b3-4a91-813b-cdf5f9cf6899" data-undisplayed="undisplayed">q28802/ProducerConsumerDemo.java</div> <pre style="overflow: visible; border: 1px solid black; border-radius: 0 4px 4px 4px;" class="px-3 pt-2 pb-1" data-ref="925dbbc4-c6b7-4b09-8162-01f83488a0ec" data-undisplayed="undisplayed">package q28802;
import java.util.LinkedList;
import java.util.Scanner;

// Write your code here...
class buffer{
	int item;
	boolean available=false;
	synchronized void produce(int value){
		try{
			while(available){
				wait();
			}
			item=value;
			System.out.println("Produced: "+item);
			available=true;
			notifyAll();
		}
		catch(InterruptedException e){
			Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
		}
	}
	synchronized void consume(){
		try{
			while(!available){
				wait();
			}
			System.out.println("Consumed: "+item);
			available=false;
			notifyAll();
		}
		catch(InterruptedException e){
			Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
		}
	}
}
class Producer extends Thread{
	buffer b;
	int n;
	Producer(buffer b,int n){
		this.b=b;
		this.n=n;
	}
	public void run(){
		for(int i=1;i&lt;=n;i++){
			b.produce(i);
		}
	}
}
class Consumer extends Thread{
	buffer b;
	int n;
	Consumer(buffer b,int n){
		this.b=b;
		this.n=n;
	}
	public void run(){
		for(int i=1;i&lt;=n;i++){
			b.consume();
		}
	}
}
public class ProducerConsumerDemo {
	// Write your code here...
	public static void main(String[] args) throws InterruptedException{
		Scanner sc=new Scanner(System.in);
		System.out.print("Enter the number of items to produce: ");
		int n=sc.nextInt();
		buffer b=new buffer();
		Producer p=new Producer(b,n);
		Consumer c=new Consumer(b,n);
		p.start();
		c.start();
		p.join();
		c.join();
		sc.close();
